---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Our Story | Eira Creek"
	description="Learn how a few bottle-fed dairy goats, generous mentors, and one exceptionally tiny Golden Guernsey doe shaped the future of Eira Creek."
>
	<header class="page-hero">
		<div class="container page-hero-content">
			<p class="eyebrow">Our Story</p>

			<h1>One Exceptionally Tiny Doe Changed Everything</h1>

			<p class="lead">
				We did not set out to become Golden Guernsey breeders. We found the breed one goat
				at a time.
			</p>
		</div>
	</header>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container story-layout">
			<div class="story-introduction">
				<p class="eyebrow">Where It Began</p>

				<h2>Three bottle babies and a simple goal</h2>
			</div>

			<div class="story-copy">
				<p>
					Our journey with goats began in 2020 with three bottle-fed dairy kids and a
					simple goal: to provide fresh milk for our family. Those first goats introduced
					us to the daily rhythms of caring for a healthy, productive herd. Over the next
					several years, we devoted ourselves to learning how to manage goats well.
				</p>

				<p>
					What began as a practical step toward greater self-reliance soon became
					something much more meaningful.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-neutral">
		<div class="container story-layout">
			<div class="story-introduction">
				<p class="eyebrow">Generous Beginnings</p>

				<h2>Welcomed into the dairy goat community</h2>
			</div>

			<div class="story-copy">
				<p>
					A neighbor and friend who raised registered Nubian goats learned that we had
					started keeping dairy goats and generously gifted us our first purebred does.
					Her encouragement introduced us to the world of registered dairy goats and
					reinforced the value of thoughtful breeding, documented genetics, and
					responsible animal care.
				</p>

				<p>
					We chose to focus on goats registered with the American Dairy Goat Association
					because registration provides a clear record of ancestry and supports more
					informed breeding decisions. It also helps us connect offspring with homes that
					value the long-term health and future of their animals.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section radar-section">
		<div class="container story-layout">
			<div class="story-introduction">
				<p class="eyebrow">Our First Golden Guernsey</p>

				<h2>Meet Radar</h2>
			</div>

			<div class="story-copy">
				<p>
					When the first Nubian kid born at Eira Creek arrived as a singleton doe, our
					friend had a singleton Golden Guernsey buckling who also needed a companion.
					She brought him to us so the two kids could grow up together.
				</p>

				<p>
					We named him Radar because of his expressive upright ears and the way he moved
					them toward every sound. Radar was our first Golden Guernsey. At the time, we
					did not know he was opening the door to an entirely new direction for Eira
					Creek.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="vanilla-section">
		<div class="vanilla-overlay"></div>

		<div class="container vanilla-content">
			<p class="eyebrow">The Doe Who Stayed</p>

			<h2>Vanilla Bean came for an afternoon. She never went home.</h2>

			<div class="vanilla-copy">
				<p>
					The following year, a set of Golden Guernsey triplets was born at our
					neighboring farm. One doeling was exceptionally small, and our friends worried
					that she might be trampled by the larger kids if left unattended.
				</p>

				<p>
					I offered to babysit her while they went grocery shopping. I fell in love with
					her almost immediately.
				</p>

				<p>
					That tiny doeling became Vanilla Bean, the foundation doe of our Golden
					Guernsey herd. Her gentle temperament, curious personality, and unmistakable
					charm gave us our first real understanding of what made the breed so special.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-neutral">
		<div class="container story-layout">
			<div class="story-introduction">
				<p class="eyebrow">The Spice Girls</p>

				<h2>One kidding season clarified our future</h2>
			</div>

			<div class="story-copy">
				<p>
					The following year, Vanilla Bean gave birth to triplet doelings. We named them
					Ginger, Saffron, and Cinnamon, and they quickly became known around the farm as
					the Spice Girls.
				</p>

				<p>
					As we spent time with Vanilla Bean and her daughters, our appreciation for the
					Golden Guernsey continued to deepen. Their intelligence, affection, confidence,
					beauty, and distinctive personalities convinced us that we had found the breed
					we wanted to build our program around.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section commitment-section">
		<div class="container commitment-inner">
			<p class="eyebrow">Where We Are Today</p>

			<h2>A commitment to the American Golden Guernsey</h2>

			<p class="lead">
				Since choosing to focus on Golden Guernseys, we have dedicated ourselves to
				learning as much as possible about the breed’s history, genetics, conformation,
				dairy qualities, development, and preservation.
			</p>

			<p>
				We have begun showing our goats and participating more actively in the Golden
				Guernsey community. We are grateful for the breeders who have shared their
				knowledge, animals, and encouragement with us, and we hope to offer that same
				generosity to others.
			</p>

			<p>
				We are excited to help shape the future of the American Golden Guernsey. Our goal
				is to strengthen the breed while remaining faithful to the qualities that make it
				so remarkable, and to help more people discover, appreciate, and fall in love with
				these goats just as we did.
			</p>

			<div class="story-actions">
				<a class="button" href="/our-herd">Meet Our Herd</a>
				<a class="button button-secondary" href="/contact">Contact Eira Creek</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page-hero {
		padding-block: clamp(7rem, 16vw, 12rem);
		background:
			linear-gradient(rgba(18, 58, 99, 0.72), rgba(18, 58, 99, 0.72)),
			url('/images/hero-goat.jpg') center / cover no-repeat;
		color: white;
	}

	.page-hero-content {
		max-width: 950px;
		text-align: center;
	}

	.page-hero .eyebrow {
		color: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.page-hero h1 {
		color: white;
	}

	.page-hero .lead {
		max-width: 700px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
	}

	.story-layout {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
		gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 8rem);
		align-items: start;
	}

	.story-introduction h2 {
		max-width: 520px;
	}

	.story-copy {
		max-width: 720px;
	}

	.story-copy p,
	.commitment-inner p:not(.eyebrow):not(.lead) {
		color: var(--color-text-soft);
		font-size: 1.08rem;
	}

	.radar-section {
		background: var(--color-secondary);
	}

	.vanilla-section {
		position: relative;
		display: flex;
		min-height: 680px;
		align-items: flex-end;
		overflow: hidden;
		background: url('/images/hero-goat.jpg') center / cover no-repeat;
	}

	.vanilla-overlay {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		background:
			linear-gradient(
				90deg,
				rgba(10, 34, 59, 0.92),
				rgba(10, 34, 59, 0.7) 55%,
				rgba(10, 34, 59, 0.18)
			),
			linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(10, 34, 59, 0.72), transparent 65%);
	}

	.vanilla-content {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
		padding-top: 8rem;
		padding-bottom: 6rem;
		color: white;
	}

	.vanilla-content .eyebrow {
		color: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.vanilla-content h2 {
		max-width: 820px;
		color: white;
	}

	.vanilla-copy {
		max-width: 720px;
		color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
		font-size: 1.08rem;
	}

	.commitment-section {
		background: var(--color-secondary);
	}

	.commitment-inner {
		max-width: 850px;
		text-align: center;
	}

	.commitment-inner .lead {
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.story-actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 800px) {
		.story-layout {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 2rem;
		}

		.vanilla-section {
			min-height: 720px;
		}

		.vanilla-overlay {
			background:
				linear-gradient(
					0deg,
					rgba(10, 34, 59, 0.96),
					rgba(10, 34, 59, 0.62) 75%,
					rgba(10, 34, 59, 0.25)
				);
		}
	}
</style>